Description: Add stub BUILD.gn for bundled libc++ when using system libc++
 When use_custom_libcxx=false (system libc++), the bundled libc++ directory
 buildtools/third_party/libc++ doesn't exist in the source tree. However,
 //build/config/BUILD.gn unconditionally references this path.
 .
 This stub provides an empty group target so GN can load the BUILD.gn file
 without errors. The actual libc++ headers and libraries come from the
 system libc++-19-dev package via -stdlib=libc++ compiler flags.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-18

diff --git a/buildtools/third_party/libc++/BUILD.gn b/buildtools/third_party/libc++/BUILD.gn
index e69de29..e1cab9d 100644
--- a/buildtools/third_party/libc++/BUILD.gn
+++ b/buildtools/third_party/libc++/BUILD.gn
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Copyright 2025 The Chromium Embedded Framework Authors. All rights reserved.
+# Stub BUILD.gn for bundled libc++ when use_custom_libcxx=false
+#
+# This file is required because //build/config/BUILD.gn references
+# //buildtools/third_party/libc++, but when using system libc++ (use_custom_libcxx=false),
+# this directory doesn't exist in the source tree.
+#
+# This stub provides an empty group target so GN can load the file without errors.
+# The actual libc++ headers/libraries come from the system (libc++-19-dev package).
+
+# Minimal valid GN file - provides empty target
+group("libc++") {
+  # No dependencies - system libc++ is used via -stdlib=libc++ compiler flags
+}
